  "definition": "Lamotrigine is a synthetic drug with antiepileptic and pain-relieving properties. It appears to work by increasing inhibitory GABA activity and may also affect sodium channels, glutamate release, and serotonin reuptake, which can reduce pain-related nerve signaling.",
